**Considering code referencing**

The developer noted that path references shouldn’t include line numbers. I think using `src/...` and phrases like "第 Lxx 行" could be the way to go. Maybe for inline references, I could use something like `[src/components/...:27]`. While the developer emphasizes not including line numbers, it seems important for user clarity. So, when I refer to review findings, it makes sense to mention file paths in monospace and keep line numbers separate. That feels like a good solution!
